# Privacy Policy – TrapSQL

**Effective date: August 7, 2026**

## Introduction

TrapSQL is a database management application developed to help users work with MySQL, MariaDB, and Microsoft SQL Server databases. This Privacy Policy explains how TrapSQL handles user information and protects user privacy.

## Data Collection

TrapSQL does not collect, store, or transmit any personal information from users.

The application is designed to operate locally on the user's computer. Database connection information, SQL queries, and database data remain under the user's control and are not sent to TrapSQL developers.

## Database Connections

TrapSQL allows users to connect to their own database servers. Connection details, including server addresses, usernames, passwords, and database content, are used only to establish connections requested by the user.

TrapSQL does not access, copy, or upload database content to external servers.

## AI Assistant

TrapSQL may include an optional AI assistant feature that can help users generate SQL queries, explain SQL statements, or assist with database-related tasks.

When the AI assistant is used, information explicitly submitted by the user may be processed by the selected AI provider, such as OpenAI or another configured AI service. Users are responsible for reviewing the privacy policies of the AI services they choose to use.

TrapSQL does not store AI conversations or submitted database information on its own servers.

## Analytics and Tracking

TrapSQL does not use third-party advertising services, tracking technologies, or analytics systems that collect personal information.

## Cookies

The TrapSQL application itself does not use cookies.

If you visit the official TrapSQL website, your browser may store standard technical cookies required by the website provider. These cookies are not used by the TrapSQL application.

## Third-Party Services

TrapSQL may allow connections to external services selected by the user, such as AI providers or database servers. These services operate under their own privacy policies.

TrapSQL is not responsible for the privacy practices of third-party services.

## Data Security

TrapSQL is designed to keep user data on the user's device. Users are responsible for protecting their computer, database credentials, and access to their database servers.

## Children's Privacy

TrapSQL does not knowingly collect personal information from children. The application is intended for users who work with database technologies and development tools.

## Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to reflect changes in the application or legal requirements. The latest version will always be published on this page.

